Z||000000||loafer87gt||07-23-2001||05:39 PM||||I received an email last night containing the SirCam virus. The message had no subject, but had the following text in the body.<P><I> Hi! How are you?<P>I send you this file in order to have your advice<P>See you later. Thanks </I><P>The message also had a infected word document attachment containing the worm. Here is some more info on the virus:<BR> <A HREF="http://news.cnet.com/news/0-1003-200-6625286.html?tag=mn_hd" TARGET=_blank><BR> <A HREF="http://news.cnet.com/news/0-1003-200-6625286.html?tag=mn_hd</A>" TARGET=_blank>http://news.cnet.com/news/0-1003-200-6625286.html?tag=mn_hd[/URL]</A>  <BR> <A HREF="http://arstechnica.infopop.net/OpenTopic/page?a=tpc&s=50009562&f=174096756&m=7090955332&r=7090955332" TARGET=_blank>http://arstechnica.infopop.net/OpenTopic/page?a=tpc&s=50009562&f=174096756   &m=7090955332&r=7090955332</A> <P>My Norton antivirus failed to pick up the virus, so be cautious and remember to be careful when opening attachments!!<P>BTW, I have received two more of the emails today so far<p>[This message has been edited by loafer87gt (edited 07-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||Levi||07-23-2001||05:52 PM||||Thanks for the warning. <P>On Friday I actually got that e-mail, and then I got 2 more of them on Saturday. But since I didn't know who it was from I didn't bother to open the attachment.||||reg||1
