Z||000013||Mach10||07-24-2001||01:40 PM||||These email viruses usually propagate by reading the addressbook of the infected computer. Thanks to MS's LOVELY "feature" of adding everyone that you've ever gotten an email from in Outlook/Outlook Express, this doesn't surprise me.<P>Beer_stud: Keep telling yourself that. Maybe it'll come true. I'm a former victim of MonkeY_A, MonkeY_B, Stoned, Stoned_B, Stonedxxx(Don't remember the variant) NATAS, and a couple of miscellaneous worms. Do you have ANY idea how much of a pain in the ass it is to rebuild your Master Boot Record manually after having your harddisk trashed? Personally, I just install command antivirus, and disable the bootup TSRs. Viruses ARE real, and they have nothing to do with the software vendors. It's just that no-one can be bothered to write a virus for Linux or Mac. (Although there are some out there... Quite nasty, actually)<BR>||||reg||13
